it's been almost 40 years since the 1984  version of stephen king's fire starter  blazed through cinemas and it was only a  matter of time in a land of infinite  remakes and reboots till firestarter  arose from the ashes the fire puns will  get worse in this series we take a look  at some of the major differences between  the old and the new so spoilers beware  and if you like this video make sure to  check out my other comparison videos  including one on stephen king's the  stand the basic plot of fire starter is  the same a young girl the daughter of  two people who underwent secret  government testing exhibits a variety of  telekinetic powers chiefly pyrokinesis  in the 84 version charlie mcgee is  played by drew barrymore and in the 22  ryan kira armstrong who you may remember  as being that creepy kid in the latest  season of american horror story drew was  about 8 when she played the role and  ryan 11. before charlie was born her  parents andy and vicki mcgee needed some  extra cash and did what any struggling  college student would do and signed up  for some completely harmless clinical  trials they'd be injected with a  mysterious compound called lot 6 and in  the 84 version we actually see these  trials in fact it's these trials where  andy and vicky first meet and yes that's  heather locklear who plays the mom who's  in the movie for about 30 seconds the 22  version glosses over this part of the  story and instead incorporates it into  the intro credits via interview footage  vicky's part in the new version is  greatly expanded and actually provides a  good foil to zac efron's andy she wants  to teach her daughter how to control her  powers while he wants her to suppress  them so the first 20 or so minutes of  the new version focuses on this family  dynamic how charlie is picked on in  school and the re-emergence of her  powers which seem to have been dormant  for the past three years the 84 version  of the story goes about this rather  differently instead immediately starting  with andy and charlie on the run and  mama firestarter already dead the  elements featuring the mom are told  through flashbacks while in the new  version everything is pretty much told  chronologically so just who exactly are  the mcgees running away from in both  versions it's a group called the shop  which is run by a branch of the us  government called dsi or the department  of scientific intelligence both are  headed by dr joseph wandless and report  to captain hollister and yes that's the  dad from that 70s show and martin sheen  in the 84 version dr wandless has a  larger role and is seen as the voice of  reason against captain hollister who  wants to weaponize children like charlie  in the new version they've made him  mentally unstable kind of like that  crazy guy who warns people you don't  want to go down that road you know he's  right but he's also crazy random  difference music in 84 is done by  tangerine dream and the new version john  carpenter if the 84 version starts with  adam and charlie already on the run then  what's going on in this new one well the  family has basically been hiding since  charlie was born in fact the shop tried  to steal the baby when it was born but  adam used his psychic powers to kill the  kidnappers and the fam has been on the  run ever since none of this is shown in  the old version this event also acts as  a good explanation for why the mcgees  don't have computers or cell phones  since they fear they could be tracked at  any moment but when charlie has a  literal meltdown at school in which he  almost toaster strudel's her teacher the  shop is notified and a special agent is  sent by the shop to bring her in what  we're leading up to here is the death of  charlie's mom in the 84 version a bunch  of shop cronies find their house and  kill her she falls out dead from a  closet in both versions but the new one  weaves in a character known as john  rainbird and the way his character goes  through the story is arguably the new  version's biggest deviation from the  past not only do they correct the  casting the 84 version saw native  american john rainbow portrayed by white  actor george c scott but his background  story and motivations are completely  different in both the book and old  version rainbird has these burn marks on  his face an injury he sustained in  vietnam but the modern version does away  with this and instead makes rain bird a  sort of secret agent under the control  of captain hollister in fact he himself  was a test subject of lot 6 even before  the compound was tested on white college  students referring to him and his fellow  native americans as expendable lab rats  his exposure to this compound resulted  in him having powers which in the old  version he does not so we have andy and  charlie on the run eventually taking  refuge with an old farmer named irv  manders in the new version andy actually  has to use his psychic powers to  convince the farmer to take them in  while in the old he's basically just a  friendly farmer who likes to take  hitchhikers back to his farm but the big  difference here is the farmer's wife who  in the new version is on some form of  life support having sustained injuries  in a car crash that her husband was a  part of although i think this is a  really cool idea to me the new version  missed out on a really heart-wrenching  scene in which charlie's powers could be  used to communicate between irv and his  wife like if i found out a kid could  communicate with my wife who i haven't  been able to talk to for years i would  be willing to protect the [ __ ] out of  that kid in the old version irv just  literally comes out of his house with a  rifle when he sees the shop and  threatens to kill them in the new  version instead of the shop showing up  it's the local police since irv has  called them hearing on the news that  andy is a wanted fugitive the police are  all taken out by rainbird who wants to  bring these two in himself in the old  version it's charlie who defeats the  shop by using her firepowers now this is  where the story really branches off in  two different directions in the old  version both charlie and andy escape  only to be tranquilized and brought back  into the shop's underground lair while  the new version sees charlie escape and  her dad used his bait to lure her back  this creates two very different  scenarios one in which charlie must  escape from captivity and a life of  being tested on to one in which she must  break into the facility to save her  father one is breaking out and one is  breaking in now in the old captivity  scenario john rainberg poses as an  orderly to gain charlie's trust he  basically wants to make it easier to  control her the new version is way  different here he's brought into dsi  custody for killing all those cops and  somehow has the power to telepathically  communicate with charlie who's miles  away i'm not sure how that exactly works  because so far in the story you've only  been able to use these powers if you can  directly look into another person's eyes  this is why you'll see rainbird blocking  his eyes behind this lamp here so that  andy doesn't use his telepathic powers  on him we'll also see members of the  shop use these special contact lenses so  they can't be manipulated by those with  powers so rain bird pretends he's  charlie's father using telepathy to get  her to come to the facility and burn it  all down that's rainbird's secret plan  here he wants revenge for what the shop  did to him charlie easily gains access  to the secret facility by burning the  [ __ ] out of an expecting dad yeah  literally a minute before this guy dies  we hear him on the phone being excited  that his wife is pregnant then he's  burnt to a crisp so charlie can get the  access card and that's another big  difference the charlie in the new  version is extremely unlikable i'm not  saying her acting is bad or anything but  she just does things so irreprehensible  that it's hard for me to connect with  her as a character like there's  literally a scene where she burns a cat  alive and there's also this other scene  which i'm pretty sure was cut from the  movie but was shown in the trailer where  she makes a bird explode now charlie  eventually finds her dad held captive by  hollister and he uses his telepathic  power to control charlie into killing  him and hollister together talk about  really messing your daughter up contrast  this to the old version where it's andy  who tries to escape with his daughter  but ends up getting shot by rain bird in  the process so in each version andy dies  just by different methods this results  in the climax of the film where charlie  goes full carry and destroys anyone in  her path now i gotta say the old version  kicks ass here it's like they put 90  percent of the budget in the final 10  minutes remember this was before cgi so  all the fire effects were done  practically and you have like flaming  dummy corpses flying about real  fireballs and charlie stopping a bullet  and making it explode in this version  charlie kills a rainbird and it's pretty  [ __ ] awesome which couldn't be  further than what happens in the new one  the shop's able to stop charlie by using  these thermal suits and a fantastic idea  turning on the sprinklers and just when  it looks like charlie's going to be  captured again rainbird shoots the  baddies and offers himself up to her  he's done unspeakable things throughout  his life and believes he should be  killed but charlie shows mercy and  simultaneously that she can finally  control this power charlie escapes with  a facility exploding behind her and  collapses in front of a nearby beach  where she's reunited with rain bird and  he carries her off into the distance  that's the end of the new version so in  the old one after her rampage killing  dozens of men she somehow hitchhikes her  way back to the manders farmstead all by  herself